  "Neutral Atoms": "中性原子",
  "Sodium (Na) has 1 valence electron. Chlorine (Cl) has 7 valence electrons. Both atoms are neutral.": "钠原子最外层有1个电子，氯原子最外层有7个电子，起始均为中性原子。",
  "Electron Transfer Begins": "电子转移示意",
  "The electronegativity difference (ΔEN = 2.23) is > 1.7, so this will be an ionic bond. Na's valence electron starts moving toward Cl.": "Na与Cl电负性差较大，示意最外层电子向Cl转移；电负性差只能辅助判断键的性质，不是绝对分界。",
  "Ion Formation": "离子形成",
  "Na loses its electron → Na⁺ (cation). Cl gains electron → Cl⁻ (anion). Opposite charges create electrostatic attraction.": "Na失去电子形成Na⁺，Cl得到电子形成Cl⁻；异号离子存在静电吸引。",
  "Electrostatic Attraction": "静电作用",
  "Na⁺ (blue glow) and Cl⁻ (red glow) attract each other due to opposite charges. Coulomb force pulls them together.": "Na⁺与Cl⁻之间存在静电吸引，动画颜色用于区分粒子，不是离子的真实颜色。",
  "Crystal Lattice Formation": "晶格排列",
  "In solid NaCl, ions arrange in a crystal lattice structure. Each Na⁺ is surrounded by 6 Cl⁻ and vice versa.": "固态NaCl中离子按晶格排列，每个Na⁺近邻有6个Cl⁻，反之亦然。",
  "Separate Atoms": "分开的原子",
  "Two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom. Oxygen needs 2 electrons, each hydrogen needs 1 electron to complete shells.": "以两个氢原子和一个氧原子示意共价键形成；这不是水的实际制备路径。",
  "Atoms Approach": "原子靠近",
  "Electronegativity difference ΔEN = 1.24 (polar covalent). Atoms are attracted to form a stable molecule.": "O与H之间形成极性共价键；动画示意靠近过程，不描述真实反应机理。",
  "Electron Sharing": "共用电子对",
  "Oxygen shares electrons with hydrogen. Shared pairs spend more time near oxygen (more electronegative).": "氧与氢共用电子对，电子云偏向电负性更大的氧。",
  "Bond Formation": "共价键形成",
  "Two O-H covalent bonds form. Each hydrogen shares its electron with oxygen, creating shared electron pairs.": "示意形成两条O—H共价键，共用电子对维系原子间结合。",
  "H₂O Molecule Formed": "水分子结构",
  "Water molecule formed with 104.5° bond angle. The bent shape and polar bonds make water a polar molecule.": "水分子呈折线形，键角约104.5°，结合极性键可解释其极性。",
  "Metal Atoms": "金属原子",
  "Iron (Fe) atoms have low electronegativity (1.83) and few valence electrons. They readily lose electrons.": "以铁为例示意金属中的正离子实与离域电子；具体电子结构比此模型复杂。",
  "Lattice Formation": "金属排列",
  "Metal atoms arrange in a close-packed crystal lattice structure. Each atom touches many neighbors.": "金属中粒子有规则排列；本动画为简化阵列，不代表铁在各温度下的真实晶型。",
  "Electron Delocalization": "电子离域",
  "Valence electrons become delocalized - they're not bound to any specific atom. They form an 'electron sea'.": "部分电子不局限于某一原子，使用“电子海”模型辅助理解金属键。",
  "Electron Sea": "电子海示意",
  "Delocalized electrons (blue spheres) move freely throughout the lattice, creating metallic bonding.": "蓝色小球示意离域电子，运动轨迹不是实际电子的精确路径。",
